{"chunk_id": "ba9e67d7e642", "text": "After the devastation of the Kurukshetra war, Arjuna encounters his sister Dussala, whose kin have been slain. She pleads for mercy for her innocent child. Moved by grief and shame over the destruction caused by Duryodhana\u2019s ambition, Arjuna condemns the cruelty of Kshatriya warfare yet relents, embracing her and allowing peace. Continuing the Ashvamedha ritual, he follows the roaming sacrificial horse until it reaches Manipura. There, his son Vabhruvahana comes humbly to greet him, but Arjuna rebukes this as unworthy of a warrior and demands battle. Ulupi, Arjuna\u2019s Naga wife and the prince\u2019s stepmother, urges the son to fight his father to fulfill duty. The resulting combat is fierce and tragic: father and son wound each other terribly, and Arjuna ultimately falls unconscious, while Vabhruvahana collapses in grief beside him.\nArjuna confronts his son Vabhruvahana during the Ashvamedha quest, provoking a duel that ends with Arjuna struck down and both collapsing.\nThemes: father-son conflict, kshatriya duty, honor and battle, provocation to fulfill duty, tragic combat", "vector": [-0.0038489196449518204, -0.007292689755558968, -0.006039473228156567, 0.013067785650491714, -0.0073956940323114395, 0.032769035547971725, -0.010932167991995811, -0.003026603488251567, -0.02234502136707306, -0.01715361513197422, 0.0004957072087563574, 0.007862646132707596, 0.005641190800815821, 0.012758773751556873, -0.009723586030304432, 0.0007579384255222976, 0.03936129808425903, -0.01525833923369646, 0.03326345607638359, -0.022056609392166138, -0.008267794735729694, -0.0067090000957250595, 3.798275793087669e-05, 0.028429130092263222, -0.02509179711341858, 0.023924417793750763, -0.0017854042816907167, -0.02610810473561287, 0.0017064345302060246, -0.009936461225152016, -0.006733034271746874, 1.1735492080333643e-05, 0.008054920472204685, 0.0037527824752032757, -0.0182111244648695, 0.019447172060608864, -0.0005111577920615673, -0.01472271